articles.body:
A workspace is either on the free plan or on a plan agreed with Caudals for a pilot or a subscription.

## The free plan {#free}

A free workspace includes:

- one AI system, connected as a website chat or an API;
- up to 50 tests per test set;
- three runs a calendar month, one at a time;
- downloads of every report as PDF, Word and CSV;
- Caudals' own models, running on Caudals' servers.

Scheduled runs, uploaded answers and the private runner are not part of the free plan. When you reach a limit, the app tells you which one, for example "The free plan includes three runs a month. Talk to us about a pilot for more."

## What Settings shows {#settings}

**Settings → General** shows **Plan and limits**: your plan and what it includes, such as how many AI systems, questions per test set and runs a month, and how many runs can go at the same time. It also lists the ways Caudals may reach your systems and whether exports and scheduling are on.

These are set by your plan or your agreement with Caudals; a workspace member cannot change them.

## Credits {#credits}

Caudals is introducing prepaid credits for pay-as-you-go use, workspace by workspace. Where credits are on for your workspace, Settings has a **Billing and usage** tab and the sidebar shows your plan and balance. Elsewhere nothing is charged in credits.

- **1 credit = €0.01 excluding VAT.** Credits pay for completed work only: engine tokens, each question your system answers, pages and documents read. Failed, retried and cancelled calls are free.
- **Before every run** you see an estimate, for example "About 270–340 credits (≈ €2.70–€3.40). You have 1,820." The range is what most runs like this one cost; the higher figure must be covered before the run starts, unless auto-recharge will cover the gap.
- **While a run works**, a few credits are held for the call in progress and released when it finishes. You pay what the call used, never more than was held.
- **If credits run out**, the run pauses with "Paused — add credits to continue". Add credits and it continues by itself.
- **Limits.** Owners can set a monthly credit limit and a per-run limit (twice the run's estimate unless they change it). A run that reaches a limit pauses until an owner raises it.
- **Alerts.** Owners get an email and everyone who sees the balance gets a notice when it is low, when credits are about to expire and when a limit is near. Choose which emails you get in Settings → Notifications.

Owners see everything in Billing and usage; editors see the balance and usage; viewers do not see billing. Purchased credits and their bonus are valid for 24 months, and the monthly free credits until the end of the month. Our [Terms of Service](https://caudals.com/en/legal/terms) describe how credits work.

## Pilots and subscriptions {#managed}

Pilots, monthly subscriptions and custom datasets are quoted on the scope of your system, with a fixed price agreed before we start, and invoiced as agreed. To discuss one, [book a call or write to us](help:getting-help).

## Where it is stored {#hosting}

The application, database, file storage and backups run on servers Caudals operates at Hetzner, in Germany. The database and file storage are not reachable from the public internet.

## Which models read it {#models}

By default, test questions are written and answers graded by an AI model that runs on Caudals' own GPU server. Your content goes to a commercial AI provider only if your workspace chooses one. Free workspaces use only Caudals' own models.

## Credentials and logins {#credentials}

API keys and tokens are write-only: Caudals encrypts them, uses them only to call your system and never shows them again. A login you save in the live browser is stored encrypted and stays until you revoke it; Caudals never receives your password.

## What Caudals asks your system {#questions}

Caudals asks only the ordinary questions in your test set. It never runs adversarial tests, such as prompt injection or jailbreak attempts, without your written authorisation.

## How long data is kept {#retention}

- Workspace content (sources, test sets, runs and reports) is kept while the workspace exists.
- Screenshots from failed website checks are deleted after seven days.
- Free test results on caudals.com are deleted after seven days.
- Backups expire after about a week.

## Shared reports {#sharing}

You decide what leaves the workspace. Shared links expire, and an owner can revoke them at any time; see [Reports, exports and sharing](help:reports-and-sharing#revoke). A copy someone already downloaded cannot be recalled.

## Delete a workspace {#delete}

Owners can delete the workspace in **Settings → Danger zone** with **Delete workspace data**. You give a reason and type the workspace name to confirm. Deletion revokes every share and credential at once, stops running evaluations, withdraws reports and deletes stored files. It cannot be undone, and access stops immediately for every member. A minimal deletion record remains, and encrypted backups expire on their normal schedule.

## Legal documents {#legal}

The [data processing agreement](https://caudals.com/en/legal/dpa) applies to every workspace without a signature; a signed copy is available on request. See also the [sub-processors](https://caudals.com/en/legal/subprocessors) and [security](https://caudals.com/en/legal/security) pages. For privacy requests, write to privacy@caudals.com.

## Help in the app {#in-app}

- Open **Help** from the account menu, or press ⌘K (Ctrl+K on Windows) and choose **Help**. Search the articles by keyword.
- The **?** next to a step opens the article about that step.
- Every article also has its own page, which you can share with a colleague in your workspace.

## Talk to us {#contact}

- Write to hello@caudals.com, or choose **Contact Caudals** in the account menu.
- For a problem with one evaluation, choose **Request operator assistance** in that evaluation's three-dot menu. It opens an email with the evaluation's name, so we know where to look.
- Book a 30-minute call from the help panel.

Tell us what you expected and what happened. Never send passwords, API keys or tokens by email: credentials belong in the app, where they are stored encrypted.

## Keep track of your work {#notifications}

The bell in the top bar lists what finished, failed or needs you (**Notifications**) and what is running now (**Activity**). Choose which notifications you also receive by email in **Settings → Notifications**.

## How we grade {#method}

The [methodology](https://caudals.com/en/methodology) explains how questions are written, how answers are graded, what each label means and what the numbers can and cannot tell you.
